z88dk-elf was born from the converter, compiler adapters, stack/location analysis, 
guarded unwinder and regression fixtures developed to support VSCode debugging 
under the z80 supported version of gdb. The intended target being z88dk compiled
C and mixed assembly Amstrad PCW CP/M programs running with the Amalia-IO gdb stub.

External toolchains, GDB, Node.js and the CDT extension are separate projects, 
not redistributed by this package, and retain their respective licenses.

This project is not an official z88dk, GNU GDB or Eclipse CDT release.
